To compute the n-th Fibonacci number modulo p, you can use an iterative approach to avoid the potential overflow issues with large numbers. Here's a JavaScript function that does this:

```javascript
function fibonacciMod(n, p) {
    if (n === 0) return 0;
    if (n === 1) return 1;

    let prev = 0;
    let curr = 1;

    for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
        let next = (prev + curr) % p;
        prev = curr;
        curr = next;
    }

    return curr;
}

// Example usage:
